# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# REDIRECTS — URL continuity across THREE generations of growthinn.co.
#
# Written 2026-10-11, from the Search Console export of 2026-10-10
# (`growthinn.co-Performance-on-Search-2026-10-10/`). Netlify / Cloudflare
# Pages format. Astro copies `public/` verbatim into `dist/` at build.
#
# ⛔ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The current build shipped with NO redirect file
#   at all, and the generations do not share paths:
#
#     gen-1  /ecommerce-development-services/*   /insights/*   /case-studies/*
#     gen-2  /services/*                         /notes/*      /work/
#     gen-3  /shopify-cro/ etc.                  /notes/*      /case-studies/*
#
#   gen-2's own `_redirects` pointed gen-1 at gen-2 targets — `/services/cro-ux/`,
#   `/audit/`, `/work/` — and NONE of those exist in gen-3. So every gen-1 URL
#   was 301-ing into a 404.
#
#   ⚠️ THE COST, MEASURED: 3,467 of the site's 4,140 impressions over 12
#   months (~84%) sit on gen-1 paths. `/ecommerce-development-services/shopify-cro/`
#   alone carries 2,541. The monthly series tracks the break exactly —
#   1,371 impressions in August, 617 in September, 21 in October.
#
# ⛔ NO CHAINS. Every rule below points at its FINAL gen-3 destination.
#   A gen-1 URL goes straight to the live page, never via its gen-2 name.
#   If a target is ever renamed, re-point every rule that aims at it
#   rather than adding a hop.
#
# ⛔ 301, NOT 302. These renames are permanent; a 302 tells search engines
#   to keep the old URL, which is the opposite of the intent.
#
# ⛔ NO BLANKET RULE TO ROOT. Google reads a mass redirect to `/` as a soft
#   404 — worse than a clean 404. The three URLs with no equivalent are
#   listed at the bottom and left to 404 deliberately, with reasons.
#
# ⚠️ THESE RULES 404 ON LOCALHOST, AND THAT IS NOT A BUG. This is a HOST
#   file: Netlify and Cloudflare Pages parse it at deploy. `astro dev` and
#   `astro preview` serve static files and 404 on any path without one.
#   ⛔ Only `curl -I` against the deployed origin is proof that a rule works.
#
# ⚠️ THE 13 `/notes/*` SLUGS ARE UNCHANGED between gen-2 and gen-3 and need
#   no rules. Only the gen-1 `/insights/*` spelling does.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


